{
  "id": "functional-independence-measure",
  "term": "Functional Independence Measure",
  "definition": "The Functional Independence Measure is an assessment scale used in rehabilitation, including a subscale commonly used to evaluate bowel-related functioning in people with neurogenic bowel problems after central nervous system injury or disease. In this context, it is used to gauge how independently a person manages bowel function.",
